--
-- Test Description
-- This test verifies the operation of ARP detection for Wake-on-LAN.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks that the ARP type field is correctly recognised.
-- * Checks that the ARP target protocol field is correctly recognised when
--   it matches the wol_ip_addr[15:0] register value.
-- * Checks the operation of the WoL enable mask.
-- * Checks that when the wol_ip_addr[15:0] register value is 0x0000 a wakeup
--   event is not generated.
-- * Checks the operation of the "wol" output.
-- * Checks that the ARP frame is recognised for both good and bad frames.
-- * Checks that the ARP frame is recognised for both VLAN and non-VLAN frames.
-- * Checks that the ARP frame is only recognised for a broadcast address.
-- * Checks that the ARP frame is only recognised when broadcasts are enabled.
--
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--  3. Send the DUT various frames to test ARP request detection for WoL:
--
-- Test 1: Good ARP that generates WoL
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a good receive ARP request frame with correct type and operation 
--     fields and a target address that matches the value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame is successfully received.
--
-- Test 2: Good ARP, but mask disabled
--     Disable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register, enable all
--     other wake up event and program the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a good receive ARP request frame with correct type and operation 
--     fields and a target address that matches the value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 3: Good ARP type, bad operation, good IP address match
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a good receive ARP request frame with correct type field and a 
--     target address that matches the value programmed, but the operation
--     does not indicate an ARP request.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 4: Good ARP type, good operation, bad IP address match (MSB)
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a good receive ARP request frame with correct type and operation 
--     fields, but the target address does not matches the MSB value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 5: Good ARP type, good operation, good zero IP address match
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register with 0x0000.
--     Send a good receive ARP request frame with correct type and operation 
--     fields and a target address that matches the value programmed (0x0000).
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 6: Bad CRC ARP that generates WoL
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a receive ARP request frame with bad CRC, but correct type and 
--     operation fields and a target address that matches the value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame dropped with a CRC error.
--
-- Test 7: Too short ARP that generates WoL
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a short (60 bytes) receive ARP request frame, but correct type and 
--     operation fields and a target address that matches the value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame dropped with a undersize error.
--
-- Test 8: Non-broadcast ARP that does not generates WoL
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a receive ARP request frame to a non-broadcast address that matches
--     specific address 1, but correct type and operation fields and a target 
--     address that matches the value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted and that the frame is 
--     successfully recognised.
--
-- Test 9: Good VLAN ARP that generates WoL
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a good receive VLAN tagged ARP request frame with correct type and
--     operation fields and a target address that matches the value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame is successfully received.
--
-- Test 10: Broadcast ARP, but broadcasts are disabled
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Disable reception of broadcasts.
--     Send a receive ARP request frame to the broadcast address with correct 
--     type and operation fields and a target address that matches the value 
--     programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted and that the frame is 
--     not recognised.
--     Receive a frame to trigger an interrupt and return the system back to
--     normal operating conditions.
--
-- Test 11: Bad ARP type ID MSB
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a receive ARP request frame to the broadcast address with incorrect 
--     typeID MSB.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted, but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 12: Bad ARP type ID LSB
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a receive ARP request frame to the broadcast address with incorrect 
--     typeID LSB.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted, but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 13: VLAN tagged, bad ARP type ID MSB
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a VLAN tagged receive ARP request frame to the broadcast address
--     with incorrect typeID MSB.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted, but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 14: VLAN tagged, bad ARP type ID LSB
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a VLAN tagged receive ARP request frame to the broadcast address
--     with incorrect typeID LSB.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted, but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 15: Bad VLAN tag, but good ARP
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a VLAN tagged receive ARP request frame to the broadcast address
--     with correct ARP typeID. Ensure that the VLAN type ID field is incorrect.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted, but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 16: Repeated ARP typeID
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a receive ARP request frame to the broadcast address with correct
--     ARP typeID. Repeat the ARP typeID as if a VLAN tag had been inserted.
--     Verify that the wol output is still asserted, and that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--     Note, because the protocol type is not checked by this implementation 
--     the frame is still seen as an ARP request.
--
-- Test 17: Good ARP type, good operation, bad IP address match (LSB)
--     Enable the ARP wake up event enable bit in the WoL register and program
--     the WoL target address match register.
--     Send a good receive ARP request frame with correct type and operation 
--     fields, but the target address does not matches the LSB value programmed.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
--  4. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states 3
bus_grant_delay 0


--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--******************************************************************************
-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      04 00080001  -- Setup speed bit.
apbrd      04 00080001  -- verify write to network config register.
apbrd      18 00000000  -- check reset value of receive queue pointer
apbwr      18 fffff000  -- write receive queue pointer
apbrd      18 fffff000  -- check receive queue pointer
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 0fffffff  -- enable all interrupts except WOL
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive



--******************************************************************************
--  3. Send the DUT various frames to test ARP request detection for WoL:
--******************************************************************************

--  check reset state of Wake-on-LAN output
pinsc(50) wol 0



--******************************************************************************
